- Story & Context: In the village of Omen-Gap, Elias the lens-grinder was obsessively perfecting a mirror meant to reflect the eclipse onto the town square when the sky turned to lead. As the temperature plummeted, his hand slipped, shattering a massive optic lens that sent splinters flying into the crowd’s wine glasses. "Do not drink the light, for the glass remembers the heat." The first notes of the band began just as the sun vanished, marking the birth of their ritual.
